  nodeTextLayers:
  - Beta cells will secrete insulin in response to glucose and other hormones in
    the bloodstream; The GLP1 receptor here (GLP1 - R) responds to one of those hormones,
    GLP1.
  - Most people with diabetes take drugs that activate GLP1-R and to help their beta
    cells secrete more insulin.
